# Project Operating System Rules

This set of rules cover the full project methodology for documentation,
feature lifecycle, and planning dispatch. Read them together; they are
designed to be applied as a unified system.

1. `operating-system/doc-system-lifecycle.md` — 4-layer doc system, artifact conventions, naming
2. `operating-system/feature-lifecycle.md` — feature types, status lifecycle, triage, rollout, post-execution review
3. `operating-system/planning-dispatch.md` — which skill to use when, triage gate, dispatch scenarios

## How to Use

When starting any task that involves planning, features, or documentation:

1. Read all three files in `operating-system/` (they cross-reference each other)
2. Apply them in order:
   - Does it need a doc? → doc-system-lifecycle
   - Does it need a feature entry? → feature-lifecycle
   - Which skill dispatches it? → planning-dispatch

## Rule Priority

- Project-specific rules override these.
- These define the **default project methodology baseline**.
